# Convex functions

There is no `src/app/api/` and no Directus. All backend lives in `convex/`.

- Import `query` / `mutation` / `action` / `internal*` from `"./_generated/server"`. Import `api` / `internal` from `"./_generated/api"`. Never `import { query } from "convex/server"`.
- Object form only, with `args` validators. Add `returns` on new functions.
- Default to `internalQuery` / `internalMutation` / `internalAction`. Promote to public only when a client hook needs it (`useQuery` / `useMutation`).
- Identity: session token on the client, validated like `getCurrentUser` in `convex/auth.ts`. Do not trust a client-supplied `userId` for authorization.
- Never return `hashedPassword`. Use a `publicUser`-style projection.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export const getCurrentUser = query({
  args: { token: v.optional(v.string()) },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    if (!args.token) {
      return null;
    }
    const userId = await validateSessionToken(ctx.db, args.token);
    if (!userId) {
      return null;
    }
    const user = await ctx.db.get(userId);
    return user ? publicUser(user) : null;
  },
});
```

Read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` before writing Convex code.
